---
import DocShell from '../layouts/doc-shell.astro';
import { docsLinks } from '../lib/nav';
---

<DocShell
   title="Verification semantics"
   summary="Verification produces structured verdicts for each criterion: pass, fail, mixed, manual-only, or not-covered. Every result clearly reports what was tested automatically and what still needs human review."
   links={docsLinks}
>
   <section>
      <h2>Three evidence categories</h2>
      <ul>
         <li><strong>Automated:</strong> the runtime has full procedure coverage and can produce a machine verdict.</li>
         <li><strong>Hybrid:</strong> the runtime gathers evidence, but a human needs to interpret part of the result.</li>
         <li><strong>Manual:</strong> the runtime provides criterion context, but the judgment requires human review.</li>
      </ul>
   </section>

   <section>
      <h2>Criterion verdicts</h2>
      <div class="mini-grid">
         <div class="stack"><div class="tag">pass</div><p>All required checks ran successfully for this criterion.</p></div>
         <div class="stack"><div class="tag">fail</div><p>The runtime collected evidence that shows a failure.</p></div>
         <div class="stack"><div class="tag">mixed</div><p>Some checks passed while others failed or produced errors.</p></div>
         <div class="stack"><div class="tag">manual-only</div><p>The criterion requires human judgment that the runtime cannot automate.</p></div>
         <div class="stack"><div class="tag">not-covered</div><p>No test procedure exists for this criterion yet.</p></div>
      </div>
   </section>

   <section>
      <h2>Level verification</h2>
      <p>
         <code>verify level</code> outputs the full criterion matrix for the requested conformance
         level. Some rows may be manual-only or not-covered even when automated checks pass,
         so the matrix gives a complete picture of conformance status.
      </p>
      <p>
         See the <a href="/workflows#verify-a-level">level verification workflow</a> for step-by-step usage.
      </p>
   </section>

   <section class="field-note">
      <h2>Interpreting results</h2>
      <p>
         A clean axe run covers static rule checks — it does not equal full WCAG conformance.
         A virtual reader transcript reflects simulated behavior — it does not represent VoiceOver or
         NVDA output. Make sure your evidence covers the same scope as the conformance claim you're making.
      </p>
   </section>
</DocShell>
